{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up","id":222481,"title":"Help a dev: Lunar round-up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-08T15:10:52-07:00","id":222481,"title":"Help a dev: Lunar round-up","content":"If you guys want to save us a couple of days of research time, it would be much appreciated. We're looking for a list of all the canonical Lunars, plus their totems/spirit shapes, if they've ever been revealed (or at least implied).<br /> <br /> thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:13:43-07:00","id":222504,"title":"","content":"I'm probably going to get in trouble for saying this, but I think it might be best not to rely on forum people to do your research for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:22:52-07:00","id":222511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222504#post222504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably going to get in trouble for saying this, but I think it might be best not to rely on forum people to do your research for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh. We'll get 75% of it right, and then spend the next little bit correcting the other 25%, and then arguing about how it should be. I'm bored, so I'll try to do some research in a little bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:23:34-07:00","id":222512,"title":"","content":"I hereby officially assign Chompy a puppy totem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:24:58-07:00","id":222514,"title":"","content":"Do you want just the ones that are currently alive in-setting or the historical ones too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:30:05-07:00","id":222519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222511#post222511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. We'll get 75% of it right, and then spend the next little bit correcting the other 25%, and then arguing about how it should be. I'm bored, so I'll try to do some research in a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you get 100% of it right, the developers have no way to be sure of that unless they do the research for themselves. Which is kind of their responsibility. If it takes a couple of days, it takes a couple of days. But what's important is that it's done right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:33:40-07:00","id":222521,"title":"","content":"Ka-kosha, Snake-Totem<br /> Seven Devil(s) Clever, Fox-Totem<br /> Anja Silverclaws, Cat-Totem<br /> Uka the Boar, er, Boar-Totem<br /> Magnificent Jaguar, Jaguar-Totem<br /> <br /> More when I get home and can leaf through my books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:35:50-07:00","id":222523,"title":"","content":"I think Sleeves of War's spirit shape might be alluded to in the chapter fiction in Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:36:52-07:00","id":222524,"title":"","content":"Well, just from Scroll of Exalts and MoEP: Lunars,<br /> <br /> Kajeha Lef : Leopard<br /> Strength-of-Many : Bull<br /> Lilith: Owl<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi: Wolf<br /> Red Jaws: Wolf<br /> Tamuz: gazelle hound<br /> Anja Siverclaws: cat<br /> Swims in Shadows: Bull Shark<br /> Madame Vert: Tree Strider<br /> Leviathan: Orca<br /> Rain Deathflyer: Hawk<br /> Silver Python: Python, presumably<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:40:01-07:00","id":222526,"title":"","content":"Lilith, owl<br /> Red Jaw, wolf<br /> Raksi, ape<br /> Strength of Many, bull<br /> <br /> (Just to point out, the signature characters were <i>not</i> remembered off-hand by anyone thus far; I take that as a sign.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:46:07-07:00","id":222529,"title":"","content":"Tad from memory (and now book skim-through), so excuse any mistakes:<br /> <br /> Anja Silverclaws, Cat<br /> Arr D'gado, Puma<br /> Faithful Pia, Cat<br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater, Eagle<br /> Heyesha Black Asp, Snake<br /> Ingosh Silverclaws, Bear<br /> Ka-Koshu, Cobra<br /> Kajeha Lef, Leopard (Scroll of Exalts) or Snake (original art piece from the Making of Exalted book)<br /> Khadarys Shadow-Dancer, has sharkfolk children but not stated as being a shark or not<br /> Lady Merta, no totem or Caste given<br /> The Last Hunter of Xaal, Spider<br /> Leviathan, Orca<br /> Lilith, Owl<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi, Goat/Wolf Hybrid thing<br /> Madam Vert, Clawstrider<br /> Magnificent Jaguar, Black Jaguar<br /> Mnalilf Nganto, Shark<br /> Muan, no totem given<br /> No Trouble Zhang, Racoon<br /> Rain Deathflyer, Eagle/Hawk (Forget which)<br /> Raksi, Ape<br /> Red Jaw, Wolf<br /> Sage of the Depths, Octopus<br /> Seven Devil Clever, Fox<br /> Silver Python, Python<br /> Strength-of-Many, Bull<br /> Swims in Shadows, Shark<br /> Tagar Frostbreath, Fox<br /> Tammuz, Gazelle Hound<br /> Ten Stripes, Tiger or Tiger Shark (Unclear)<br /> Uka the Boar, Boar<br /> <br /> Sure someone ninja'd me on most of these.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 08-08-2014, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:54:02-07:00","id":222536,"title":"","content":"That whale-totem woman from Savage Seas...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:54:27-07:00","id":222538,"title":"","content":"Dark Eyes; I think he's the spider guy, isn't he? Well, whatever, he's mentioned on page 39 of <b>Exalted: the Lunars</b>, if you want to go look it up.<br /> Tammuz, gazelle<br /> Muan, who might be a wolf or a cat or a deer; page 54 of <b>Exalted: the Lunars</b><br /> Swift Pinions, raptor of some sort<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi, wolf<br /> Leviathan, whale of some stripe<br /> Kambaka, ape","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:55:18-07:00","id":222539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222519#post222519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you get 100% of it right, the developers have no way to be sure of that unless they do the research for themselves. Which is kind of their responsibility. If it takes a couple of days, it takes a couple of days. But what's important is that it's done right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's kind of it. Depending on their purpose, it may <i>not</i> be important that it be complete.<br /> <br /> You could think of it as a matter of prioritization. Depending on why they want the list (candidates for appearances in art pieces, short descriptions of example characters, reminders of character types and totems they've done before, etc.), they've probably already got a good idea of most of the ones who would be on it. What they want is quick references and reminders for those that may have slipped their minds. I would imagine a perfectly complete list would be ideal, but not at all necessary for their purposes. It's the sort of list they don't strictly <i>need</i> for the purpose -- and, more to the point, really can't justify taking time away from other work to do it themselves. So they weigh the options of doing without or finding another way. Particularly with the Exalted Wiki still down, crowdsourcing is a fine option.<br /> <br /> I'd also expect they will be doing some research of their own, in any case. This just speeds up that process. &quot;Oh, yeah, I can't believe I forgot that character,&quot; is one reaction to seeing a name. Meanwhile, &quot;Who was this character again?&quot; can be followed by dropping a name into the search bar for a few PDFs, which either elucidates things or doesn't. In the latter case, they shrug and move onto looking at the other names that don't feel familiar.<br /> <br /> I think they did something similar at least once, a few months ago. Asking for a list of all the gods mentioned in the books, I believe...? Not to say, &quot;Someone did X before, therefore it's fine to not question doing X now,&quot; but it suggests they've tried it and found the results sufficiently worthwhile to do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:00:08-07:00","id":222542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222538#post222538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Eyes; I think he's the spider guy, isn't he? Well, whatever, he's mentioned on page 39 of <b>Exalted: the Lunars</b>, if you want to go look it up.<br /> Tammuz, gazelle</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Eyes' spirit shape, in 2E, is a simhata. He's in COTD East.<br /> Tamuz is a gazelle hound, which I guess is a kind of southern wild dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:00:18-07:00","id":222543,"title":"","content":"From the compasses I managed to find:<br /> <br /> Dark Eyes: Simihata<br /> Rakshi: Red baboon<br /> No Trouble Zhang: Racoon<br /> Mnalif Nganto: Shark<br /> Red Coral Manta: Unknown, possibly manta ray. (First Age)<br /> Swims in Shadows: Shark<br /> Sage of the Depths: Octopus<br /> Shining Ocelot: Ocelot, probably (first age)<br /> Den\u2019Rahin: Unknown (first age)<br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater: eagle<br /> <br /> I know a few of these have been mentioned already but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:13:12-07:00","id":222549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222542#post222542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Eyes' spirit shape, in 2E, is a simhata. He's in COTD East.<br /> Tamuz is a gazelle hound, which I guess is a kind of southern wild dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changed your tune eh?<br /> <br /> Okay, lemme see what I can find.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:16:10-07:00","id":222552,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's what I did. I went through every PDF I own from First Edition, and did a search for the word Lunar, and made notes and references to whatever I found that looked like a character. I only used the PDF search function, and I did NOT do Exalted: Lunars. Books that I have done: Aspect Book Earth, Bastions of the North, Blood and Salt, Creatures of the Wyld, Cult of the Illuminated, Exalted: The Autochthonians, Exalted, the Fair Folk, Savant and Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Mnemon duelled a Lunar while in the Wyld hunt. Tell: Coat of feathers? Silver eyes? Mnemon beheaded him.Aspect Book Earth, P. 42<br /> <br /> Den\u2019Rahin. Husband of Twilight Caste Tenrae. Came to Ondar Shambal after it's first fall.Renamed it Whitewall. Bastions of the North, P 14.<br /> <br /> Arvida of the Crescent Eye, wild patron to the Haslan tribes, the Bear Woman, killed by Immaculate monks in RY 412. Bastions of the North, P. 85<br /> <br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater, No Moon, patron to the Haslanahsa and Haslanosha, Bastions of the North, P. 86<br /> <br /> Lunar Flintbeak Nightingale disperesed a Wyldfog in RY 726. Bastions of the North, P. 87<br /> <br /> One of the Grandmothers of the Haslanti League is Keen-Eyed Snowcat, of the No-Moon caste. Bastion of the North, P. 103<br /> <br /> Blood and Salt P. 32. The Dwelling of the Serpents Who Walk Like Men refers to an ancient Lunar, who was probably a snake.<br /> <br /> Blood and Salt, P. 34. Khadarys Shadow-Dancer is a survivor of the Usurption, and owns a First Age Manse, Rushing Waters, at the bottom of a lake<br /> <br /> Blood and Salt, P. 58, 105. Mnalilf Nganto, a pelagothropic, power-questing Full-Moon Lunar has a pirate fleet somewhere in the west. Admiral of Post Pwoona<br /> <br /> Blood and Salt, P. 82. Sadana, Lunar Mother of Serpents<br /> <br /> Creatures of the Wyld 2, P. 8. Lunar Hero Crimson Unity freed the bear killers. <br /> <br /> Cult of the Illuminated P. 120, Faithful Pia, companion to Jak, the night Caste Solar.<br /> <br /> Exalted: The Autochthonians: P. 6. Ten Stripes Lunar.<br /> <br /> Exalted: The Fair Folk: P. 83. Ka-Koshu, doesn't like Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Exalted: The Fair Folk: P. 295. Swan is married to an Owl-shape Lunar named Lillith.<br /> <br /> Raksi, no explanation needed. Leviathan, no explanation needed.<br /> <br /> Savant and Sorcerer, P. 122. Lunar general Shu-lin Seven Fangs<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:20:05-07:00","id":222553,"title":"","content":"First Edition<br /> <br /> Introduced in Core:<br /> Lilith: Owl<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi: Wolf or goat.<br /> Magnificent Jaguar: Jaguar<br /> <br /> Introduced in Scavenger Sons<br /> Dark Eyes: Tiger?<br /> <br /> Introduced in Savage Seas:<br /> Lady Merta: No totem listed<br /> <br /> Introduced in Time of Tumult:<br /> Ten Stripes: Maybe jaguar, maybe marsh dragon. 2e likely had him/her as some kind of shark or siaka.<br /> Mithra: ?<br /> <br /> Introduced in Caste Books:<br /> Unidentified near Coral: whale?<br /> Unidentified foe of Yurgen: snow ape/yeti?<br /> Nala or her successor: Cheetah?<br /> Flourish Deathcry: ?<br /> Raiton: Raiton<br /> Light Sinks Deep: ?<br /> Unnamed Opponent of Horakinis: Panther/general big cat<br /> Smaragdine Serpent-eye: Two-striped forest pitviper<br /> Unnamed Lunar with Blood-red Forelock: ?<br /> Stone Bear: Bear<br /> Grandfather Frost: Some kind of pack creature, presumably a wolf<br /> <br /> Introduced in Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded<br /> Sleeves of War: ?<br /> <br /> Introduced in Exalted: the Lunars<br /> Muan: Wolf<br /> Uka the Boar: Boar<br /> Seven Devil Clever: Fox<br /> Red Jaws: Wolf<br /> Strength of Many: Bull<br /> Raksi, Queen of Fangs: Ape<br /> Kambaka: Ape<br /> Leviathan: Orca<br /> Tamuz: Gazelle Hound<br /> Anja Silverclaws: Cat*<br /> Swims in Shadows: Shark (going by the look of the sharkfolk named for him, a white shark; for some reason, Scroll of Exalts listed it as a bull shark, with art that was indicative of a pointer)<br /> Kajeha Lef: Art from E:tL indicates snake, Scroll of Exalts goes with a leopard.<br /> Ka-Koshu: Some kind of snake, likely desert-dwelling.<br /> <br /> Introduced in Manacle and Coin<br /> Tekia Blue Water: ?<br /> <br /> Introduced in Blood and Salt<br /> Sadana, Mother of Serpents: Some variety of snake.<br /> Khadarys Shadow-Dancer: Freshwater shark<br /> Mnalif Nganto: Listed as barracuda, but has shark features and themes.<br /> <br /> From Aspect book: Wood<br /> Lunar from the Battle of Tamrin Plain: Elk<br /> Lunar of the Hundred Waterfalls Manse: Wolf<br /> Suki Yommi (deceased creator of Death At the Root): ?<br /> <br /> Introduced in material cut from Creatures of the Wyld<br /> Crimson Unity: ?<br /> <br /> Introduced in the Player's Guide<br /> Heysha Black Asp: Likely in the name<br /> Rhazahd Va'deen, the Maelstrom of Blades: Spider<br /> Ombato Hammer Horn: Rhino<br /> Him What Waits: ?<br /> Companion of Him What Waits: Not sure if Lunar; given the ambiguous appearance, may even be Luna.<br /> <br /> Introduced in Exalted: the Autochthonians<br /> Aslan: I'm guessing Lion.<br /> <br /> Introduced in Cult of the Illuminated<br /> Faithful Pia: Cat*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* You have no idea how tempting it was to list that as &quot;fine, too.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-08-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:44:02-07:00","id":222560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222542#post222542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Eyes' spirit shape, in 2E, is a simhata. He's in COTD East.<br /> Tamuz is a gazelle hound, which I guess is a kind of southern wild dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changed your tune eh?<br /> <br /> Okay, lemme see what I can find:<br /> <br /> Anointed Starfall B/W, Treatise Page 19, Totem Unknown<br /> Night Eyes, Masters of Jade Page 10, Totem Unknown<br /> Ghost Wolf Masters of Jade Page 43 Presumably a Wolf, or some kind of Shark<br /> Alcina Masters of Jade Page 55 Totem Unknown, Looks to be Lacan Mercer's Mate<br /> Raksi, Wonders of the Lost Age Page 23, Ape<br /> Admiral Leviathan Wonders of the Lost Age Page 28, Orca<br /> Ma-ha-Suchi, Wonders of the Lost Age Page 158, Goofy Goat/Wolf Hybrid<br /> Kinich Makar, N/A, Croc or Gator Totem<br /> <br /> <br /> Bleh. What a sad list. Hope there was something useful in there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T18:22:53-07:00","id":222646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222512#post222512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hereby officially assign Chompy a puppy totem</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that work, anyway? Could you have a totem that's like, &quot;old giraffe&quot;? &quot;Middle-aged beetle&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T19:20:37-07:00","id":222682,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one has mentioned the <a href=\"http://meluran.deviantart.com/art/Spry-Attack-52400102\" target=\"_blank\">Ibex Lunar from the 2E core.</a><br /> There's also this weird <a href=\"http://meluran.deviantart.com/art/CHASE-132151109\" target=\"_blank\">Lion/alligator/octopus</a> Chimera, although I'm not sure if that counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T19:35:06-07:00","id":222717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222646#post222646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would that work, anyway? Could you have a totem that's like, &quot;old giraffe&quot;? &quot;Middle-aged beetle&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your true forms all age at the same rate, normally. Scarring, unhealed dismemberment and other permanent damage is shared visibly between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:03:26-07:00","id":222725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222646#post222646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would that work, anyway? Could you have a totem that's like, &quot;old giraffe?&quot; &quot;Middle-aged beetle?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it's ever explicitly stated, but I believe one's totem animal is a specific example of a totem animal, not all variations of a type of animal. You're always going to turn into the same black cat with white spots, not Garfield and Heathcliff and...uh...Sabrina the Teenaged Witch's creepy animatronic cat...and whatever else...<br /> <br /> Really lost my momentum there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:27:41-07:00","id":222749,"title":"","content":"Has someone already mentioned Echidna the Chimera who is kind of MoW's friend/mate/pet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:33:53-07:00","id":222752,"title":"","content":"I know there was a Lunar mentioned in Masters of Jade - the Cake-Eating Lunar. I don't have the book on me; was her Totem ever mentioned and/or implied?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:52:53-07:00","id":222769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222749#post222749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has someone already mentioned Echidna the Chimera who is kind of MoW's friend/mate/pet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimerae are changing substantially across editions, though. Echinna the Faceless won't be lacking a face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T21:25:03-07:00","id":222780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222752#post222752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there was a Lunar mentioned in Masters of Jade - the Cake-Eating Lunar. I don't have the book on me; was her Totem ever mentioned and/or implied?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure at what point &quot;Chompy&quot; became the go-to moniker when talking about her (it didn't take long, though), but this is as close as we've gotten on a totem:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222512#post222512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hereby officially assign Chompy a puppy totem</div> </div> </div> </div>Make of that what you will. I personally go for &quot;Vance put on the pair of special glasses he made for himself that cause him to see everyone as puppies.&quot; ... Also, how would one handle that as a Charm, Artifact, or other effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T21:32:47-07:00","id":222782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222646#post222646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would that work, anyway? Could you have a totem that's like, &quot;old giraffe&quot;? &quot;Middle-aged beetle&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone needs to provide you with the Vance quote on what constitutes a puppy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:10:49-07:00","id":222816,"title":"","content":"There is Jade-Beaked Ukari, an Alabatross Lunar who lives in the South, mentioned in in Splinters of the Wyld page 12<br /> and Master Garudo, Splinters of the Wyld page 19, who Exalted during the Shogunate, though it doesn't say what his spirit shape is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:22:24-07:00","id":222826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222725#post222725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe it's ever explicitly stated, but I believe one's totem animal is a specific example of a totem animal, not all variations of a type of animal. You're always going to turn into the same black cat with white spots, not Garfield and Heathcliff and...uh...Sabrina the Teenaged Witch's creepy animatronic cat...and whatever else...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b858rOO21Fw\" target=\"_blank\">Sorry, I'm just under a Geas to link to THIS [NSFW!] whenever someone mentions Sabrina and Salem!</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 08-09-2014, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T03:08:35-07:00","id":223061,"title":"","content":"There was a rather good list of published characters on the Exalted wiki before it went down. Just saying.<br /> <br /> Luckily I am me and keep obsessive notes on this sort of thing. Here are some of the less well known ones from first edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Caste Book Dawn:</b><br /> Unnamed Lunar, sea monster shape of some sort, possibly Pelagial Dragon, destroys whaling fleets.<br /> Unnamed Lunar, snow ape shape, attacks the Bull of the North.<br /> Flourish Deathcry, unknown spirit shape, observes a female Dawn Caste.<br /> <br /> <b>Caste Book Night:</b><br /> Unnamed Lunar, possible Tyrant Lizard spirit shape, leads a pack of Wyld Mutants and fights prisoners to death for sport.<br /> Stone Bear, unknown spirit shape (bear?) meets Harmonious Jade.<br /> <br /> <b>Caste Book Twilight:</b><br /> White Leopard, leopard spirit shape, mentor to the Twilight caste Gannet.<br /> Unnamed Lunar, panther spirit shape, challenges Horakinis.<br /> (First Age) Unnamed Lunar, albino lion, mentioned.<br /> <br /> <b>Caste Book Zenith:</b><br /> Raiton, likely raiton spirit shape, rescues Wind.<br /> <br /> <b>Creatures of the Wyld</b><br /> (Shogunate) Sorrowful Light, unknown spirit shape, traps Arad the Hunter<br /> <br /> <b>Creatures of the Wyld - Bonus Material</b><br /> Crimson Unity, unknown spirit shape, elder, freed the Bear Killers from Raksha control, plans to unite an army to conquer the Threshold.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspect Book Wood</b><br /> (Usurpation) Suki Yommi, unknown spirit shape, created Death at the Root through ritual suicide.<br /> <br /> <b>The Autochthonians</b><br /> Alsan, perhaps lion spirit shape, rallies defenders against Autochthonian invasion.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult of the Illuminated</b><br /> Faithful Pia, cat spirit shape, casteless Illuminated Lunar.<br /> <br /> <b>Kingdom of Halta</b><br /> (Deceased) Arphene, unknown spirit shape, student of Silver Python, now a ghost.<br /> The Last Hunter of Xaal, spider spirit shape, former student and lover of Raksi.<br /> Arr D'Gado, probably mountain lion spirit shape, hunts ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>Savage Seas</b><br /> Lady Merta, unknown spirit shape, elder, has concealed her Exalted status for centuries, runs a large and successful trade house in the West.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood And Salt</b><br /> Sadana, Mother of Serpents, snake spirit shape, elder returned to claim her ancient beastmen domain. Possibly an imposter.<br /> Khadarys Shadow-Dancer, shark spirit shape, First Age elder, remains in her subterranean manse with her beastmen children.<br /> Mnalilf Nganto, shark spirit shape, pelegiathrope, elder, leads a semi-independent Lintha fleet called the Tumult's Prowl.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aaaaaand others have already done it better. That'll teach me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-09-2014, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:05:57-07:00","id":223462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=222752#post222752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there was a Lunar mentioned in Masters of Jade - the Cake-Eating Lunar. I don't have the book on me; was her Totem ever mentioned and/or implied?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a picture. I think she might've been some kind of reptile because she kinda had slit eyes but..It's really hard to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:00:52-07:00","id":223640,"title":"","content":"Oh,there's also Thorn Moon-and-Sun, the Lion-totem Lunar from Rose Sun-and-Moon's writeup at the back of Castebook: Eclipse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T19:20:45-07:00","id":223769,"title":"","content":"Hesha Black Asp?<br /> <br /> Isn't that the name of the Lunar who had a thing for Harmonious Jade? The chick with the weird accent?<br /> <br /> Serpent form, presumably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T07:56:39-07:00","id":224103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=223462#post223462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a picture. I think she might've been some kind of reptile because she kinda had slit eyes but..It's really hard to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of reptiles don't actually have that kind of eye structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T08:02:36-07:00","id":224104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=224103#post224103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of reptiles don't actually have that kind of eye structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is irrelevant, since artists tend to add &quot;snake eyes&quot; to reptilian things anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T08:42:02-07:00","id":224164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/222481-help-a-dev-lunar-round-up?p=223769#post223769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hesha Black Asp?<br /> <br /> Isn't that the name of the Lunar who had a thing for Harmonious Jade? The chick with the weird accent?<br /> <br /> Serpent form, presumably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which makes me wonder if all the Lunars in the 1E Player's Handbook are considered canonical and worth mentioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T09:02:23-07:00","id":224175,"title":"","content":"Best to be thorough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}